  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_9ccc23ca0ac34c63a79334320423aa7b",
      "statement": "The `manifold-eval` console entry is the shipped before/after GRPO eval driver; it is registered in `pyproject.toml` as `manifold-eval = \"manifold.eval.cli:main\"` and owns the policy inference, export-bridge call, and CLI-level orchestration.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://pyproject.toml#L85-L85",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4e14760ecfd84118d3afe45b321dcf26a1ddf99f8c5c2696ee1a775908304225:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/cli.py#L244-L341",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3c328b864f164673d7e5f38a4f0e64ea01abac1fefcbcc60010936d9cabe76c1:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d669fd9bd54f4bfebf045c2495b0eb6a",
      "statement": "The evaluation policy (JiT vs ControlNet) is inferred from the before directory's `model_index.json` `pipeline_class` field via `_pipeline_class_of`; there is no evaluation mode flag. Unknown pipeline classes fail fast with the supported list.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/cli.py#L132-L165",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2dff360e6a172ed549e51f000b8f245d179bcd3d36ec24864623bfe719ecde6a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b70e93af9a0d421ab9fd0e6b6b6e15a6",
      "statement": "`BeforeAfterEval` creates the same-noise pairing contract by giving each pipeline a fresh generator on the UNet's device with the same `seed` (JiT) or by drawing one noise tensor and passing the same tensor to both pipelines' `sample_latent` (ControlNet); the source latent, real target latent, spacing, contrast labels, and Heun step count stay fixed.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L104-L143",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6cf0b11994fc48ad13a89e14f61648f0447a2a34c8f4c7fd4cd8035af44ca05f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L163-L222",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:6672c956226841ba3570b7ec0296d8a355d3178c5a56b874daba633bb819a01c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_090ef2abdce145ec8998f9beef14f359",
      "statement": "`BeforeAfterEval._decode_normalize` decodes each latent through a fresh `LatentDecoder` (with `vae.eval()`) under `torch.inference_mode` and then applies the shared `min_max_to_unit` so the before/after/real volumes all live in `[0, 1]` and the paired-fidelity metric can assume `data_range = 1.0`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L82-L94",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:321a8fdec1fc36142709a26b0755561321573b61e005bbc81a77b60d56696667:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/pipelines/pipeline_utils.py#L26-L42",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c7258dad146f718103147a3e91f612e9fef1a9c0e881968db7dfe7825d59308b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e6279248b0724746a8d93523ea914cf0",
      "statement": "`PairedFidelityMetrics` composes MONAI's `PSNRMetric(max_val=1.0)` and `SSIMMetric(spatial_dims=3, data_range=1.0)` (composition, not inheritance), batch-means both outputs, and requires `generated.shape == real.shape`; PSNR is `+inf` for identical volumes and SSIM is bounded by MONAI's metric.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired.py#L34-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:63ba2b62f6a540d4a824f5d4e19571e2699658897e9a0f2bacac56064883a963:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c4cc2c027307465597f49a8c48faae82",
      "statement": "`SliceGrid.render` writes one 2.5D three-plane PNG per sample: rows are the three orthogonal center slices (xy/yz/zx, axis D→xy, H→yz, W→zx) and columns are the per-policy volumes (`before | after` for JiT, `before | after | real` for ControlNet); the PNG is written atomically via `tmp + os.replace` so an interrupted render cannot leave a truncated file.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/slice_grid.py#L37-L91",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:28cf1ee9add7cbacfc296b86cd76ec6a374452aac6127822cffb3edda253960b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_49cb738fdde14df8b6e04bb9057a0636",
      "statement": "`ComparisonPageBuilder.build` produces a self-contained HTML report: it reads `metrics.json` and (for JiT) the training runs' `metrics.csv` series, embeds the generated curves and slice grids as base64 PNG data URIs, writes the page atomically (`tmp + os.replace`), and renders a clearly-marked pending slot when `controlnet=None`; the API is library-only and not registered as a console entry.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/comparison_page.py#L235-L246",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e17d31fc0a735cf59f1e6b7b9c2b6eed6f661b4ced76fa372276c1bea7d06f8d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/comparison_page.py#L80-L106",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:54d9bbfe18316ae482578f84e7b745e4653ad774ba7d6017ebaf57c7bb4f2103:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a57fe90250144757adcb6d5f127e4d63",
      "statement": "The `metrics.json` written under the eval output dir records `policy` (`jit` or `controlnet`), `seed`, `num_inference_steps`, `num_samples`, the grid basenames (so the report remains portable after the eval dir is moved), and for the ControlNet policy the `before` and `after` blocks each carrying `{psnr, ssim}`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/before_after.py#L227-L237",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4c70f30c45c606b4f6eb1b582c32fad57d67cacec20f925cb71a6540f66203d7:"
        },
        {
