          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:4bc1b412704c861903038d0871e9cda22355ef8efd0ee65e40bb2e9ee2ffd4a7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b8d00477ef9d494da5759e6da984d620",
      "statement": "The eval CLI loads a probe pipeline from the before native export and uses its UNet/VAE/scheduler (and optional `controlnet`) as the components `export_to_native` mutates in place to bake the after checkpoint into `<output>/after_native`; both sides are then reloaded as fresh `from_pretrained` pipelines so the before export's weights stay pristine.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/cli.py#L260-L286",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ac613e21755943574961a7e095cec32c8170099bef7943ba8da3225dfee4856b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/export.py#L39-L116",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b7d1a99b193c6c25345d9fb903637eed8dde374da566641672693fd52aecf40c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1bfc404cdab045ce87ea5eaa992d69e5",
      "statement": "The ControlNet eval path reuses the training data stack read-only: `build_brats_pair_manifest` → `_train_val_manifests` → the warmed paired latent cache (disk hits only — the eval never encodes), applies the before export's `vae.scaling_factor` verbatim (never re-estimated), and refuses to run on an empty held-out split.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/eval/cli.py#L176-L241",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ba5c509c9677d61909fbc2dbb59ce8de6eaf9c5ba32f9e6fbf1834692ef9b293:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b541c99257674fbe89334c49b30e1cd8",
      "statement": "The supervised ControlNet in-training paired-fidelity monitor is shipped: `PairedFidelityCallback` (in `manifold.metrics`) rolls a fixed paired subset under fixed seeded noise through the module's own `controlnet_rollout`, VAE-decodes generated and real target, normalizes both via `min_max_to_unit`, scores them with `PairedFidelityMetrics`, and logs `val/psnr` / `val/ssim` via two `torchmetrics.MeanMetric` instances attached to the module; all work runs under `inference_mode`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/__init__.py#L14-L29",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:379bbe8a2d6309109a6417dc827e3ff7604f442f5d76067845ea4dbd6a1136f6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired_callback.py#L54-L217",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b36a46cc010177414379aeee09d2f80cf856680eba2f204c2b6793ba56647574:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_21a7f9fe12b6478abbe2d0b8a44a88fe",
      "statement": "`PairedFidelitySpec` (in `manifold.training.callbacks`) is the `@dataclass(frozen=True)` registry spec for the monitor with knobs `subset_size=8`, `every_n_epochs=1`, `num_inference_steps=None`, `seed=0`, and `logged_metrics = frozenset({\"val/psnr\", \"val/ssim\"})`; only the supervised `controlnet_cli` shell registers it under the name `paired_fidelity` and includes it in the default callback list — other shells (JiT, GRPO, reward) do not register it, so a `--callbacks paired_fidelity` on those paths fails fast with `KeyError` at resolve.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/paired_fidelity.py#L36-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b98d6d123a126579faa0f2cbbe14477221dce42a80bf53998cfb5aac342c361a:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/controlnet_cli.py#L168-L188",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:944cb6e1cc0d0c339d50f767d103dc5428e22850faa595393f4705d07393abd0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7c3d0ff0f4c54c02bbf99b893be84f15",
      "statement": "The supervised `controlnet_cli` populates `CallbackContext.inference_recipe = {\"num_inference_steps\": int(num_inference_steps)}` from the `controlnet.num_inference_steps` knob; `PairedFidelitySpec.build` reads `num_inference_steps` from there when the per-callback knob is `None` (recipe-primary) and a per-callback value overrides the recipe.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/callbacks/paired_fidelity.py#L60-L74",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:082267d3ee966bacee6ed4f36d82f7b18cdfc1bdb8fb0f67938a6d0feaa256a6:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/training/controlnet_cli.py#L172-L183",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b01bd7df459543ad33d9a286fbfaa54b25260b64d2e6a5e120cf431077dec97b:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4ddd36299c6144328f7556976f6303f8",
      "statement": "The in-training paired-fidelity monitor is observe-only: it never drives checkpoint selection (the supervised shell keeps the checkpoint monitor on `val/x0_mae` via the hand-appended `LatentX0MAE`), never contributes loss, never touches the optimizer or EMA, and its DDP safety test (`tests/test_paired_fidelity_ddp.py`) verifies no-hang, identical `val/psnr`/`val/ssim` across ranks, and that the checkpoint monitor stays on `val/x0_mae`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired_callback.py#L83-L84",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f553cd60d9e5d58484c740ff428caa5cbceef56e8637ab18a598c96967ce67ff:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_callback_registry.py#L255-L265",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8f2c776422b80a85c666d1541fe3486332628aa2e374e67a8dcec906c141df79:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_paired_fidelity_ddp.py#L19-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bb1a558ae1294084763ac1a15733c0dc9035300d5a32efe9a6fbb4cd3506d73c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ee14a47ec4584f7cbe2205c07936b739",
      "statement": "Under DDP, every rank runs the in-training monitor on the same fixed paired subset redundantly (DDP-synchronized weights + identical seeded noise + identical input ⇒ identical result), so the cross-rank reduction is just Lightning's torchmetrics sync on the logged `MeanMetric`s — no FID-style sharding, no error-rendezvous machinery, and the collective-count invariance (ADR-0030) holds trivially.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/manifold/metrics/paired_callback.py#L23-L28",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ba6a13830858b38c8b9c8557d0b6a81db7e3310eca473cc171473a75217acf4d:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://tests/test_paired_fidelity_ddp.py#L19-L70",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:bb1a558ae1294084763ac1a15733c0dc9035300d5a32efe9a6fbb4cd3506d73c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6ad4973dcd7348b7b41f16e4da76a85e",
      "statement": "The ControlNet-GRPO extension of the in-training paired-fidelity monitor is the deliberate ADR-0037 follow-up and is NOT yet shipped: the GRPO path must (a) release the blanket `forbidden_callbacks={\"fid\": ...}` for `paired_fidelity` only (its rationale does not cover paired rollout), (b) keep the VAE on the rollout device for the monitor's decode, (c) wire `PairedFidelitySpec` into the GRPO default callback set with `inference_recipe` populated from the GRPO recipe's paired-rollout step count, and (d) add focused DDP + registry tests mirroring the supervised precedents. Until then `manifold-train-grpo --native-dir <controlnet>` does not log `val/psnr` / `val/ssim`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docs/adr/0037-controlnet-fidelity-in-training-monitor.md#L49-L62",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d538eece28bba4970b3c213023d757d3e9d1fc1589d04a8d52a23f5565e27af0:"
        },
        {
